-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",110,{
[3489]="70046C52\n1\tCollect ripe blackberries (total: 10)\tBerries can be found along the coastline of the Cape of Belfalas. You should collect berries.\n2\tTalk to Cranniel\tCranniel is located near the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas. You should share some of the berries you collected with Cranniel.\n",
[3490]="70006E13\n1\tCollect dire Warg hides (total: 6)\030Collect harrow weed (total: 6)\tBoth dire Wargs and harrow weed can be found in the eastern plains of Nan Amlug. In order to make armour for the Suuri-lehmä, Mauno has asked you to gather hides from dire Wargs and some harrow weed.\n2\tTalk to Mauno\030Collect Harrow-weed (total: 6)\030Collect Dire Warg-hide (total: 6)\tMauno is at the camp of the Suuri-lehmä. You have gathered enough Warg hides and the harrow weed that Mauno needs to cure them. You should take them to Mauno as soon as possible.\n",
[3491]="70071631\n1\tFree captured Beltáni (total: 10)\tKûrmi fears that the Ordâkhai have captured some of the Beltáni and taken them to Wither-watch. You should travel to Wither-watch and free any captured Beltáni you find.\n2\tTalk to Kûrmi\tYou have freed many captured Beltáni from the Ordâkhai at Wither-watch. You should return to Ahâba and talk to Kûrmi.\n",
[3492]="7003E73D\n1\tFind the Treasure Hunters' Camp\tThe Treasure Hunters' Camp can be found within the city gate of Fornost, south-west of the city itself, far to the north in the Fields of Fornost. You should find the Treasure Hunters' Camp and meet Colbert there.\n2\tSpeak with Colbert\tColbert is at the Treasure Hunters' Camp in northern Fornost. You should speak with Colbert.\n",
[3493]="7000EDE6\n1\tSummon and defeat Delucheleg\tKibilzahar lies to the north-west of Kuru-leiri. Nicca told you that some evil power has trapped fell spirits within the bodies of wights in Kibilzahar. Only the warmth of fire can banish them. He has told you to re-kindle the ancient fires that the dwarves once used to heat the ancient fortress. He also warned you of an evil lord who haunts that place, and to be ready to face him should you go there again.\n2\tTalk to Arre in Kuru-leiri\tArre is at Kuru-leiri, south-east of Kibilzahar. Having defeated Delucheleg, the Gaunt-man responsible for raising the wights, you should return to Arre and tell him of your discoveries and battles.\n",
[3494]="7002AC69\n1\tDisperse Wintry Weather (total: 4)\tWintry Weather can be found to the north-east of Winter-home. Daley Utteridge wants you to help the less fortunate of Winter-home by driving off the harsh cold that accompanied the arrival of frost grims in Frostbluff.\n2\tTalk to Daley Utteridge\tDaley Utteridge is in Winter-home. You should return to Daley Utteridge with news of your success.\n",
[3495]="7001931C\n1\tBring the iron collar to Ovorlas\tOvorlas is at the Elf-camp on the northern edge of Nen Hilith. You should bring the collar to Ovorlas and see if it means anything to him.\n",
[3496]="7002BFF6\n1\tBring the collar you found to Twiga at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tTwiga is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands. You should bring this collar to Twiga at once.\n",
[3497]="70020BAA\n1\tBring the collar to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan, south-west of Gavar Cadlus. You should bring the collar you found to Saeradan for his examination.\n",
[3498]="70062C9C\n1\tCollect craban wings (total: 8)\tAdan Rhuvyg has asked you to collect craban wings from the gardens of Lintrev. Lintrev is in the Stoor-vales.\n2\tReturn to Adan\tYou should bring the craban wings to Adan Rhuvyg. Adan is in Lintrev.\n",
[3499]="700033FD\n1\tBring the ancient chalices to Tobold Leafcutter\030Collect ancient chalices (total: 10)\tThe Great Barrow is at the heart of the Barrow-downs, beyond the Dead Man's Perch in the southern Barrow-downs. Tobold Leafcutter has asked you to gather ancient chalices from the Great Barrow located in the heart of the Barrow-downs.\n",
[3500]="7006BFA4\n1\tCollect berries (total: 5)\030Collect red wild-flowers (total: 3)\030Collect yellow wild-flowers (total: 3)\tKishâtu has asked you to gather various plants nearby in Urash Dâr.\n2\tReturned to Kishâtu with the various plants\tReturn to Kishâtu with the plants you have collected for her.\n",
[3501]="7006B608\n1\tCollect papyrus reeds (total: 6)\tPapyrus reeds can be found in the marsh near Mehêtur in Ambarûl.\n2\tBring the papyrus reeds to Sûlmur\tYou have collected papyrus reeds. You should return to Sûlmur near the barn at Mehêtur.\n",
[3502]="7006C941\n1\tCollect metal shields (total: 6)\030Defeat sand-sifters (total: 8)\tSigênik has asked you to travel to Sûr Zugub, south-east of Western Khanâg, and collect any abandoned metal shields you find. He would also like you to slay the resident sand-sifters while you're there.\n2\tBring the metal shields to Sigênik in Western Khanâg\tYou have collected metal shields and defeated sand-sifters. You should return to Western Khanâg to give the shields to Sigênik.\n",
[3503]="7004BEAA\n1\tCollect tribute from those in Fushaum Bal North (total: 6)\tYou should collect tribute from those in Fushaum Bal North.\n2\tTalk to the Khundolar Commander\tThe Khundolar Commander can be found at Fushaum Bal North. You should talk to the Khundolar Commander.\n",
[3504]="7000978A\n1\tTalk to Hal Gamgee\tHal Gamgee can be found in Oatbarton centre. Nibs Chubb has asked you to speak with Hal Gamgee about the wolves.\n2\tBring the elk-meat to Hal Gamgee\030Collect elk-meat\tYoung Greensward-hind can be found grazing in the old orchard just north of Oatbarton centre. Hal Gamgee suggested you hunt some elk to provide bait for the wolves then return to him.\n",
[3505]="70065F22\n1\tRegister for the competition with the judge\tYou have chosen to compete in a competition to help determine the best forester in all of Chetwood - right now. Speak to the judge to let them know that you are ready to compete. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tWait for others to register for the competition\tNow that you are registered for the event, you will need to wait at the Chetwood lumberyard for other competitors to join the event.\n3\tWait for the judge to say go\tAll the entrants are present and the judge is preparing to start the event. Wait for her to say 'go'.\n4\tCollect a forester's axe from the competition table\tYou first need to collect an axe so that you can chop wood and then cure skins. Hurry now. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tCollect stacks of unrefined wood ([see journal]/5)\tLog piles along Old Bauman's hovel are set up for harvesting. Take your axe and collect five stacks of unrefined wood from the piles there. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tDeliver the refined wood to Aldith\030Refine stacks of wood at the competition bench ([see journal]/5)\tMake your way to the competition table beneath the tree in the centre of the camp and refine wood with the forester's axe. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n7\tCollect unrefined skins from the bear carcasses behind Bauman's hovel ([see journal]/5)\tYou refined the wood, successfully. Now, collect hides from the bear carcasses behind Bauman's hovel. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n8\tDeliver the refined hides and axe to Aldith\030Cure skins at the competition hide stretchers ([see journal]/5)\tWith the skins collected, it is time to move on to the curing them. Make your way to the stone wall on the far side of the camp and cure skins at the hide stretchers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n9\tSample three beverages from local taverns ([see journal]/3)\tWith the hides completed, you now need to make your way to the bench beside the house and sample three brews from local taverns. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n10\tCollect a caber to carry for the event\tWith those tasty beverages consumed and sloshing in your stomach, the real test begins. Collect a caber. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n11\tPass through the first markers\tCarry the caber through the first set of markers in the Chetwood lumberyard. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n12\tPass through the second markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n13\tPass through the third markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n14\tPass through the fourth markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n15\tPass through the fifth markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n16\tPass through the sixth markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n17\tPass through the seventh markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n18\tPass through the eight markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n19\tPass through the ninth markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n20\tPass through the tenth markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n21\tPass through the eleventh markers with the caber\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n22\tPass through the twelfth markers with the cabers\tCarry the caber to the next set of red markers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n23\tCarry the caber to the final blue markers to complete the race. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n24\tReturn to the judge to claim your prize\tReturn to the judge and speak to them about your efforts in the event.\n",
[3506]="7006868B\n1\tHang up flyers... but place them poorly ([see journal]/16)\tEzôti has asked you to place flyers advertising his show all around the Upper Ward. But because Ezôti is terrible, do not do a good job. Place flyers in poorly visible spots around the Upper Ward.\n2\tDoes Ezôti need so many flyers posted?\tYou have placed a number of Ezôti's flyers. That is enough, and you should burn the rest in a fire.\n3\tThrow the remaining flyers into a fire on the south-eastern corner of the Grand Market\tInstead of distributing more flyers for Ezôti, you have decided to burn them in a fire. The open flame on the south-eastern corner of the Grand Market in the Upper Ward should suffice.\n4\tTalk to Ezôti in the Upper Ward\tYou have no more flyers left to place. Will Ezôti wonder how you accomplished the task so quickly? Probably not.\n",
[3507]="7004DA72\n1\tDefeat Orc hunters (total: 10)\030Defeat Orc ambushers (total: 10)\tOrcs can be found along the Forest River, between Felegoth and Loeglond. You should defeat the Orc ambushers and hunters that have come down from the Green Mountains.\n2\tTalk to Lorndúr\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should talk to Lorndúr.\n",
[3508]="7006569D\n1\tDiscover the snow-beast camp\tRavenous snow-beasts have been drawn down their mountain's snowy peaks by the commotion at Aban-bazan.\n2\tDefeat snow-beast slashers (total: 8)\030Defeat snow-beast flingers (total: 6)\tRavenous snow-beasts have been drawn down their mountain's snowy peaks by the commotion at Aban-bazan.\n3\tTalk to Irzeben\tYou should let Irzeben know that you have defeated many snow-beasts.\n",
[3509]="70057E44\n1\tCollect beeswax from hives (total: 5)\tLimael's Vineyard is located to the north-west of Celondim. You can find beeswax from the hives near the vineyard's entrance.\n2\tDeliver the beeswax to Gairil\tGairil is working at the Celondim docks to the south. You should bring the beeswax to him.\n3\tSet the lantern onto the river\tGairil has given you one of the lanterns he crafted earlier. You should set the lantern down onto the river.\n",
[3510]="700272C4\n1\tTalk to Huwela near the road to Tâl Methedras\tHuwela awaits you near the road to Tâl Methedras, north of the Rohirrim scout-camp. Léofward told you to meet with the Dunlending scout, Huwela, regarding the Old Woman of the Mountain.\n2\tTalk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tSaeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp, south of the road to Tâl Methedras. Huwela told you of a path she found leading up Methedras and instructed you to bring the information to Saeradan.\n",
[3511]="7001D0D2\n1\tDefeat Commander Athdurub\tAthdurub patrols the woods of Gathbúrz. Rodelleth has asked you to hunt down and defeat the Warg-rider Athdurub, commander of the Wargs of Gathbúrz.\n2\tTalk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad\tRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz. You should return to Rodelleth with tidings of Athdurub's defeat.\n",
[3512]="7001D0CD\n1\tDefeat Commander Fikthrug\tFikthrug is at Bûrzkala, directly north of Thangúlhad. Rodelleth has asked you to find and defeat the Orc-commander Fikthrug.\n2\tTalk to Rodelleth in Thangúlhad\tRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz, south of Búrzkala. You should return to Rodelleth with news of your victory.\n",
[3513]="700173AB\n1\tDefeat Commander Târsh (quantity: see journal)\tCommander Târsh can be found in the School of Tham Mírdain, south-east of the Elf-refuge of Echad Mirobel. Commander Târsh, a pride-filled uruk-hai, leads the forces of the White Hand in an attempt to gain information of old from the School in which he has established his host. Gelirwen wishes you to enter the School and face down this brute with the aid of a small fellowship.\n",
[3514]="7002CCFC\n1\tTalk to Orion\tBy completing this quest, you will earn Commendations to be spent on PvMP rewards and advancement.\n",
[3515]="7002CCFD\n1\tTalk to Orion\tBy completing this quest, you will earn Commendations to be spent on PvMP rewards and advancement.\n",
[3516]="700077F4\n1\tTalk to Falco Greenhand at his farm\tFalco Greenhand's farm lies to the south-west of Gammy Boggs' farm. Gammy Boggs, the local town gossip, has asked you to find out why Falco's garden is failing.\n2\tTalk to Gammy Boggs at her farm\tGammy Boggs is at her farm, north-east of Falco Greenhand's farm. Falco Greenhand did not want to trouble you with his problems and asked you to tell Gammy Boggs to stop nosing about.\n",
[3517]="7002BFB9\n1\tTalk to Nár\tNár is in the library at Zudrugund. You have spoken with Frithgeir and confirmed to yourself that Saruman was lying when he spoke of killing these dwarves.\n2\tTalk to Frithgeir\tFrithgeir is in Zudrugund. You have spoken with Nár, who seems to be fine, as normal as he ever is. You should return to Frithgeir.\n",
[3518]="7002733B\n1\tTalk to Gwynna in Tûr Morva\030Talk to Olwen in Tûr Morva\tGwynna and Olwen can be found in Tûr Morva. Maelona told you that some of her fellows are distrustful of hobbits, having never seen one before, and you should tell them stories of your homeland.\n2\tTalk to Maelona in Tûr Morva\tMaelona is in Tûr Morva. Maelona will want to speak with you once you have regaled Gwynna and Olwen with tales of your homeland.\n3\tTalk to Penrod in Tûr Morva\tPenrod, the first Brehur of Lheu Brenin, is in Tûr Morva. He has been asking for you. Maelona told you to speak with Penrod now that you have reassured her friends Gwynna and Olwen.\n",
[3519]="7004D096\n1\tTravel to the gates of Erebor\tErebor is in the northern end of the Dale-lands. You should travel to Erebor to speak with the dwarves there.\n2\tTalk to Víglund\tVíglund and the crowd stand before the gates of Erebor, in the northern end of the Dale-lands. You should talk to Víglund about the dwarves gathered around the statue.\n3\tExamine the axe\tYou should examine the axe embedded in the statue at the gates of Erebor.\n4\tExamine the rust spot\tYou should examine the rust spot found at the gates of Erebor.\n5\tTalk to Víglund\tVíglund the guard can be found at the gates of Erebor. You should tell Víglund your conclusion about the axe.\n6\tComplete the Under The Mountain quest arc to continue\030Talk to Órug\tYou should continue assisting the Dwarves of Erebor. The Trail of Rust quest arc will continue after completing the Under The Mountain quest arc which begins with Órug in Erebor.\n7\tTalk to Víglund\tYou should speak with Víglund, the guard at the gates of Erebor.\n8\tTalk to Rúni\030Talk to Spall\030Talk to Fróthi\030Talk to Mágsal\030Talk to Belgur\tYou should speak with Lore-masters Rúni, Spall, Fróthi, Mágsal, and Belgur in Erebor.\n9\tTalk to Górsim\tGórsim can be found in Erebor. You should speak with Górsim about viewing the teeth of the dragon Scatha.\n",
[3520]="7004CF33\n1\tSearch Gwígar\030Search Glad Thaw\030Search Imnagath\030Clear spider webs (total: 12)\030Defeat spiders in Eryn Lasgalen (total: 6)\tKnown spider dens can be found throughout Eryn Lasgalen. You should search the woods and remaining spider-dens for spiders.\n2\tReturn to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in the halls of Felegoth. You should return to Thranduil.\n",
})
